# Working on this pangol project

- One file = one route in `src/routes/`: `health.get.ts`, `posts/[id].get.ts`.
- Every route declares `auth`, schemas for its inputs, and `response`.
- Ownership belongs in `owner`, with `load` providing `c.resource`. Never move it into the handler.
- Failed ownership checks return 404, so callers cannot discover other users' records.
- Never skip validation or response filtering. Mark secrets `.private()` and use model `.public()` for responses.
- Use `t.money` for money, never floating point.
- Run `npm run check` after every change, then `npm test` before committing.
- Security changes need both positive and negative tests. Never weaken a test to pass.
- Keep handlers synchronous when possible; avoid per-request allocation and unnecessary `async`.
- `src/auth.ts` denies all credentials until connected to a real session provider. Test auth is only in `test/`.
